                      seon.fx-test/a-write-back-answers-the-bytes-on-disk}}
 {:seon.task/name "merge-trains-off-as-decided"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #19. DECISIONS (Root's calls on R3's questions): octopus merges stay off (:seon.config.merge/max-running 1) until one combined test run of all octopus members, the par-200 hang and root memory growth with concurrent merges are fixed. The code says 8: seon.reconcile/default-max-merging (reconcile.clj:21-25) went from 1 to 8 in b7459c3, whose message says octopus merges are off by default, and nothing writes :seon.config.merge/max-running (seon.task/boot-tx, task.clj:88-92, writes only the agent config key), so every root runs octopus merges of up to 8. Correct: the default is 1; boot-tx writes both config keys as facts on main so the config value in force is a recorded fact a person can read (my.root/problems or the dashboard), and an octopus merge is turned on by writing the fact. Deletes the code default as the source of truth (the schema default in resources states it)."
